UNIT adopt_kept_content
LANG rust
PRIMARY-SHA256 f12abd39c819e36f544857da0f077f9d078ddb864b0e67ccf6ab80e83e8b7ecc
SIG pub fn adopt_kept_content(unmanaged: &str, managed: &str) -> Vec<String>
ABI crate shape: the artifact is a LIBRARY crate ([lib], src/lib.rs exporting pub fn adopt_kept_content) — no main, no
  I/O, no binary, no unsafe, no dependencies. The verifier generates its own harness crate from the abstract SIG and
  depends on the artifact by path; compiling that harness against this SIG is the signature check.
ABI text = &str (UTF-8; iterate as chars = code points); list[text] = Vec<String>. Every pinned set is BMP and no
  rule counts characters beyond "at least one", so code points and UTF-16 units agree. No error path: no Result, no
  Option, no panic.
ENVELOPE narrowing: an unpaired surrogate half has no &str form, so such inputs are outside this language's envelope;
  no oracle vector carries one.
MECHANISM no regex crate (zero dependencies): realize BEGIN, END, HEADING, LIST, the fence tests and RUN, the R6
  mask, cut and unmask by hand over chars. HEADING by hand: after 1-6 '#' (the next char not '#') the rest R must start with a
  BLANK; let k = max(1, one past the LAST NOTDOT in R); heading iff k < R's length and R[..k] is all BLANK. BEGIN by
  hand: try every "<!--" from the left; it qualifies when followed by zero or more BLANK, "rederive:begin" and then not
  a WORD char; let e = the end of "rederive:begin" and q = the first "-->" at or after e; it wins when q exists and no
  "<!--" starts at any index in [e, q); the cut ends after that "-->". ONE-LINE FENCE: the trimmed
  line starts and ends with "```", has at least 7 chars, and no NOTDOT. R6 and R7: test for '\u{0}' or '\u{1}' first (the raw,
  uncut branch; the raw KEY is '\u{2}' + the fragment byte-for-byte); in the mask branch every token is the mask's own,
  so index the span list directly. R9's contiguous test: Vec::windows over the managed list (no window when it is
  shorter than the item's list). Fence KEY LINES: a Vec built from the opener plus the non-blank middle lines only when the
  item has two or more lines and its last line CLOSES it; a one-line item only when it is a ONE-LINE FENCE; else empty. The std predicates are NOT the pinned sets: char::is_whitespace /
  str::trim / split_whitespace use Unicode White_Space, which wrongly includes U+0085 and excludes U+FEFF — write
  is_blank as a match over BLANK_RS and trim with trim_matches(is_blank). str::lines strips every CR before LF — split
  on '\n' only and remove at most ONE trailing '\r' per pass (R1 and R2 are two passes, on both texts). Digits in
  MARKER and in the unmask are ASCII only (is_ascii_digit); START is ASCII A-Z (is_ascii_uppercase), '`', '(' or
  '\u{0}', never char::is_uppercase. KEY lowercases each prose piece separately with str::to_lowercase (the Unicode
  default full mapping, final sigma decided within the piece) (asterisks kept), writes each code span as
  '\u{1}' + its text unchanged + '\u{1}', then collapses BLANK runs. PROSE LISTs are Vec<Vec<String>> (R9 is a contiguous
  window test), the BLOCK KEYs a HashSet<String>. WORD (BEGIN's boundary) is ASCII only
  (is_ascii_alphanumeric or '_'), never char::is_alphanumeric.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED charset BLANK_RS = '\u{9}' '\u{A}' '\u{B}' '\u{C}' '\u{D}' '\u{20}' '\u{A0}' '\u{1680}' '\u{2000}'..='\u{200A}' '\u{2028}' '\u{2029}' '\u{202F}' '\u{205F}' '\u{3000}' '\u{FEFF}' CITED the primary BLANK pin, spelled as Rust char literals and one inclusive range
PINNED charset NOTDOT_RS = '\u{D}' '\u{2028}' '\u{2029}' CITED the primary NOTDOT pin
PROVENANCE rederive@c7b0916ed08a cli/lib/adopt.mts — this file states the crate shape, the type mapping and the std-library traps only; no behavior.
